OL,3,GNEWSAExplosives team called to rail
OL,4,Aline as trains disrupted
OL,5,
OL,6,FPassengers faced disruption after
OL,7,Ftrains were cancelled when an object
OL,8,Fsuspected to be unexploded ordnance was
OL,9,Ffound near a rail line.
OL,11,FNorfolk Police was called at 09:52 BST
OL,12,Fafter workers found the suspicious
OL,13,Fobject near Thetford.
OL,15,FA spokesperson for the Ministry of
OL,16,FDefence said an Army explosive ordnance
OL,17,Fdisposal team responded to the incident
OL,18,Fand identified the item to be a
OL,19,Fnon-ammunition item, which was later
OL,20,Freduced to scrap.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
